{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the integer \\( n \\) such that \\( 0 \\leq n < 1399 \\) and \\( n \\) is the multiplicative inverse of 160 modulo 1399, we need to find \\( n \\) such that:\n\n\\[ 160n \\equiv 1 \\pmod{1399} \\]\n\nThis means we need to find \\( n \\) such that \\( 160n - 1399k = 1 \\) for some integer \\( k \\). This is a linear Diophantine equation, and we can solve it using the Extended Euclidean Algorithm.\n\nFirst, we apply the Euclidean Algorithm to find the greatest common divisor (gcd) of 160 and 1399:\n\n1. \\( 1399 = 8 \\cdot 160 + 159 \\)\n2. \\( 160 = 1 \\cdot 159 + 1 \\)\n3. \\( 159 = 159 \\cdot 1 + 0 \\)\n\n","prefix_end":582,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,7546,17767,308,1124,8,1741,429,17767,220,15,1124,273,80,308,366,220,16,18,24,24,1124,8,323,17767,308,1124,8,374,279,12557,65266,27949,315,220,16,21,15,59864,220,16,18,24,24,11,582,1184,311,1477,17767,308,1124,8,1741,429,1447,78045,220,16,21,15,77,1124,57317,220,16,1124,79,2593,90,16,18,24,24,92,1124,2533,1986,3363,582,1184,311,1477,17767,308,1124,8,1741,429,17767,220,16,21,15,77,481,220,16,18,24,24,74,284,220,16,1124,8,369,1045,7546,17767,595,1124,568,1096,374,264,13482,7767,5127,38357,23606,11,323,582,646,11625,432,1667,279,40565,21963,50078,40325,382,5338,11,582,3796,279,21963,50078,40325,311,1477,279,12196,4185,49109,320,91289,8,315,220,16,21,15,323,220,16,18,24,24,1447,16,13,17767,220,16,18,24,24,284,220,23,1124,50853,220,16,21,15,488,220,16,20,24,1124,340,17,13,17767,220,16,21,15,284,220,16,1124,50853,220,16,20,24,488,220,16,1124,340,18,13,17767,220,16,20,24,284,220,16,20,24,1124,50853,220,16,488,220,15,1124,692,785,44858,374,220,16,11,892,3363,220,16,21,15,323,220,16,18,24,24,525,6162,81,545,11,323,458,27949,6724,13,4695,582,990,279,40565,21963,50078,40325,311,3158,220,16,438,264,10601,315,220,16,21,15,323,220,16,18,24,24,1447,383